   "text": {
    "L1": "India has summer, the monsoon, autumn, winter and spring.",
    "L2": "Seasons are not caused by Earth being closer to the Sun.",
    "L3": "Earth's axis is tilted as Earth travels around the Sun each year.",
    "L4": "In June, our half leans towards the Sun, so sunlight falls more directly.",
    "L5": "The days are longer too, giving more hours of heating.",
    "L6": "In December, our half leans away, so light slants and days are shorter.",
    "L7": "The Earth is actually closest to the Sun in early January, during India's winter.",
    "L8": "Seasons also bring changes in nature: frogs appear in monsoon and many birds arrive in winter.",
    "L9": "Tap the statement that explains why seasons change."
   },
